    "text": "{\"anomaly_detected\": true, \"confidence\": 0.85, \"anomalies\": [{\"category\": \"bridged_nets\", \"components\": [\"IC1\", \"L2\", \"R2\", \"Q2\", \"U5\", \"C13\", \"C12\", \"U6\"], \"pins\": [\"IC1.C1\", \"L2.2\", \"R2.2\", \"Q2.2\", \"U5.28\", \"U5.29\", \"C13.1\", \"U6.1\"], \"nets\": [\"BAT+\", \"+3V3\", \"Net-(IC1-SW)\"], \"observed\": \"The regulator's output side and the battery/input side are on one net. L2 pin 2 (the output end of the 1.0 \u00b5H inductor), IC1 FB (C1), R2 pin 2, Q2 pin 2 (source), the SKW92A 3.3VD pins U5.28/U5.29 and C13 pin 1 all appear on the BAT+ net. No +3V3 net appears in the netlist, so the 3.3 V rail is shorted to the battery rail. Only L2 pin 1 sits on the SW node, so the buck output is never separated from BAT+.\", \"expected\": \"The FAN53610 output (L2 pin 2) should be the +3V3 rail, separate from BAT+ (battery/VIN). FB should sit on +3V3, and the SKW92A 3.3VD pins, R2, Q2 source and C13 should be on +3V3. The spec says: \\\"SW (pin B1) \u2192 L2 (1.0 \u00b5H \u2026) \u2192 +3V3 output rail\\\" and \\\"FB (pin C1) \u2192 +3V3 directly\\\".\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"1\\\") (name \\\"BAT+\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"IC1\\\") (pin \\\"C1\\\") (pinfunction \\\"FB\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"L2\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") ... (node (ref \\\"U5\\\") (pin \\\"28\\\") (pinfunction \\\"3.3VD\\\")\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`FB` (pin C1) \u2192 `+3V3` directly (fixed-output part; this is the standard connection for a fixed-voltage FAN53610 variant).\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`+3V3` rail destinations: SKW92A module power pins (`U5.28`, `U5.29` \u2026), keyboard `U4.2`, microSD `J2.4`, the gate pull-up `R2` \u2026, and the EPD power-switch MOSFET `Q2`'s source.\"}], \"impact\": \"The SKW92A's 3.3 V pins, the keyboard, the SD card and the display power switch are tied to the raw battery/USB input (about 4.2 to 5 V) instead of a regulated 3.3 V. This over-voltages and likely destroys the SKW92A module and other 3.3 V parts. The regulator's feedback is also tied to its own input, so regulation is lost.\", \"confidence\": 0.85}]}",
